  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Triptersinin A and L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain, mediated through a series of targets. Triptersinin A is identified as a target of G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1, which in turn is a target of (1S)-2-Cyclohexen-1-ol and Lophenol, both of which target L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain. Similarly, Triptersinin A is also a target of G2/mitotic-specific cyclin B1, which is also a target of Mollicelline K, which targets the same enzyme. These findings indicate that Triptersinin A may interact with L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain through multiple indirect pathways, possibly through different metabolic or signaling mechanisms. The scores for these relationships are consistent, suggesting a plausible biological connection. However, the exact nature of the interaction remains uncertain, and further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct relationship between Triptersinin A and L-lactate dehydrogenase C chain.",
